                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Although conceptually wonderful, this game has flaws that spoil the fun. \n\nI almost feel a sense of conflict with the design; the simplicity of placing lights to guide your path is met with difficult level pathing and frustratingly grindy attempts to replace all your lights upon dying or misclicking a lantern. \n\n[h1]Gameplay[/h1] \nYou're given a small number of lanterns to place in a dark room, revealing parts of the surrounding area. You then manouver your character through this dark room, overcoming obstacles such as spikes and bottomless pits (these will kill you) to reach the black square at the end of the level. \n\n[h1] Pros: [/h1][list]\n[*] Effective and interesting gameplay concept. \n[*] The music (acoustic strings) is melodious and soothing. It's quite a subtle and nice background noise. \n[*] Controls are simple and serviceable. \n[*] Shadow and lighting effects are executed fairly nicely.[/list]\n\n[h1] Cons: [/h1] [list]\n[*] [b]Level design[/b]. Even in clear lighting, there are some jumps and obstacles that are very punishing when they don't need to be. Trying to overcome jumps in clear sight distracts from the challenge of [i] visibility [/i].\n[*] [b]Resets[/b]. Upon dying or misplacing a lantern (in a wall for instance) you're forced to reset the level and place your lights all over again. Nevermind how long you spent trying to get your lantern placements perfect. If you didn't die so many times per level, I don't think this would be an issue.\n[*] [b]Too few lights[/b] to place. A difficult jump or obstacle is that much harder without lighting- it makes sense that you'll spend time fumbling in the dark, but the levels should allow for that with the number of lights you're given.[/list]\n\nI finished this game by taping a piece of plastic over my monitor and marking on the plastic where perfect lighting could be achieved. I used a new sheet every level to avoid confusion and despite this... sophisticated piece of engineering, the spikes [i]still[/i] killed me in dark areas.\n\nIf you're on the fence, I recommend [strike]holding out for a sale[/strike]. Otherwise, pick it up if you enjoy trial and error or think your patience can endure the frustrations. If you can, I'm sure you'll find more fun in this than I did.\n\nEdit: Visibility has since gone F2P so I might recommend giving it a couple minutes to sate your curiosity. While this doesn't change the arguments made in the review, it's a nice gesture from the developers nonetheless.",
